    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Grammar: du or Sie?",
     "md": "**du** = informal *you* (one person). **Sie** = formal *you* — always written with a capital **S**.\n\n- **du**: family, children, friends, often colleagues\n- **Sie**: people you don't know, older people, boss and clients, shops, restaurants, offices\n\nThe verb changes too:\n\n- {de:du wohnst} · {de:Sie wohnen}\n- {de:du kommst} · {de:Sie kommen}\n- {de:du heißt} · {de:Sie heißen} (*heißt*: the stem already ends in *ß*, so only *-t*)\n\nSmall **sie** (not at the start of a sentence) means *she* or *they*.\n\nDon't worry: Germans are happy that you, as a beginner, speak German at all. Usually the **older** person offers the *du*: {de:Wollen wir uns duzen?}"
    },
